`,c.jsxs(n.p,{children:[c.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Formal Legal Opinions"})," are authoritative written opinions issued by the General Secretariat on specific questions of law arising under the Charter, conventions, statutes, regulations, or other instruments of the Organization. They are addressed to organs, Contracting Parties, officials, or expert bodies of the Organization."]}),`
`,c.jsxs(n.p,{children:[c.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Advisory Notes"})," are informal guidance documents issued by the Office of Legal Affairs on procedural and interpretive questions of general application. They do not bind the Organization but represent the considered view of the Office on the matter addressed."]}),`
`,c.jsxs(n.p,{children:[c.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Advisory Opinions of the Internal Court of Arbitration"})," are judicial opinions delivered by the Court at the request of the General Council, the Secretary-General, or the Technical Nominations Board, in accordance with Article 32, paragraph 1(g), of the Charter. Advisory opinions of the Court are published in the ",c.jsx(n.a,{href:"/legal/registry#judicial-registry",children:"Judicial Registry"}),". Where the requesting parties have agreed in advance to accept them as decisive, they are binding."]}),`
